{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Scattered and dispersed among the peoples.</b> That each man is separated from his brother — all of it is evil, and not only are their laws different, but they do not keep the laws and statutes that the king commands, and behold, every people keeps them except them." "<b>It is not fitting</b> — it is not a correct thing, or it is of no benefit."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Resolved the feminine singular היא as referring to the situation described; the syntax is compressed and Ibn Ezra's argument moves quickly through three clauses."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:52.167976718Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}